Qt
--

The Qt libraries and plugins in this package are unmodified builds of
Qt @BLAIRQT_QT_VERSION@ by The Qt Company, used under the GNU Lesser General Public
License version 3: LGPL-3.0.txt, which builds on the GNU General Public
License version 3: GPL-3.0.txt.

B.LAIR_QT links Qt dynamically. You may replace the Qt libraries in
this package with your own build of Qt @BLAIRQT_QT_VERSION@, modified or not:
put your libraries in place of these (on Windows the Qt6*.dll files and
the plugin folders next to blairqt.exe; on macOS the frameworks and
plugins inside blairqt.app/Contents). On macOS, sign the app again
afterwards, or it will not start:
    codesign --force --deep --sign - blairqt.app

The complete source code of Qt @BLAIRQT_QT_VERSION@:
https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/@BLAIRQT_QT_MAJOR@.@BLAIRQT_QT_MINOR@/@BLAIRQT_QT_VERSION@/single/

Qt contains third-party components under their own licenses, listed in
"Third-Party Code Used in Qt" in the Qt documentation:
https://doc.qt.io/qt-@BLAIRQT_QT_MAJOR@.@BLAIRQT_QT_MINOR@/licenses-used-in-qt.html

Qt is a registered trademark of The Qt Company Ltd. B.LAIR_QT is an
independent project, neither affiliated with nor endorsed by The Qt
Company.


FFmpeg
------

Video is decoded by the Qt Multimedia FFmpeg plugin, which uses the FFmpeg
libraries that come with Qt @BLAIRQT_QT_VERSION@, built by The Qt Company and included
unmodified. FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License version 2.1 or later; this package uses it under version 3
(LGPL-3.0.txt). Its source code: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html, and
the version and build Qt uses: "FFmpeg" in "Third-Party Code Used in Qt",
linked above.


Microsoft Visual C++ runtime (Windows zip only)
-----------------------------------------------

vc_redist.x64.exe is Microsoft's installer for the Visual C++ runtime,
included unmodified as Microsoft permits for programs built with
Visual Studio. It is covered by Microsoft's own license terms, which
the installer shows before it installs anything.
